DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260626T080000Z
DTEND:20260626T120000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail Marathon and Heavy Half
DESCRIPTION:A high-altitude marathon starting at 10\,200 feet and climbing to 13\,185 feet at Mosquito Pass. It is part of the legendary Leadville Race Series and is known for its extreme elevation and mining-town history.
LOCATION:6th and Harrison\, Leadville\, CO 80461
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bubbleicious-bubble-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260627T120000Z
DTEND:20260627T160000Z
SUMMARY:Bubbleicious Bubble Run
DESCRIPTION:A non-competitive 5K fun run filled with foam bogs and bubble tunnels. Designed to be a moving celebration of joy\, the event features music\, a post-run party\, and is pet-friendly. Participants can walk\, jog\, dance\, or skip through the course.
LOCATION:TBD (Location emailed to participants prior to event)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:slacker-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260627T080000Z
DTEND:20260627T120000Z
SUMMARY:Slacker Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Slacker Half Marathon features a thrilling downhill course starting at 10\,880 ft elevation at the base of Loveland Ski Area and descending to 8\,400 ft through a mix of dirt and paved roads. The course passes through wetlands\, natural waterfalls\, views of the Continental Divide\, and historic mining sites. Finish line and post-race festivities are held in City Park in Georgetown with locally crafted beer\, freebies\, and entertainment. No strict time limit; water stations remain open until the last racer finishes (usually by 1:30 p.m.).
LOCATION:Loveland Ski Area\, Georgetown\, CO 80444
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alderfer-trail-race-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260627T070000Z
DTEND:20260627T110000Z
SUMMARY:Alderfer Trail Race
DESCRIPTION:Trail race in beautiful Alderfer/3 Sisters Park offering 5K and 10K courses. Check-in starts at 6am at Wulf Rec Center. EPRD shuttles runners/spectators to The Alderfer Barn. Last shuttle departs at 6:40am. Day of registration increases price by $5.
LOCATION:Alderfer/3 Sisters Park\, Evergreen\, CO 80439
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-marathon-heavy-half-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260627T063000Z
DTEND:20260627T103000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail Marathon & Heavy Half
DESCRIPTION:The nation's toughest marathon. The Life Time Leadville Trail Marathon and Heavy Half presented by La Sportiva takes trail runners through the historic mining district's challenging trails to Mosquito Pass (13\,185 feet) - the highest continuous pass in the country and the highest trail marathon in the USA. Marathon: 26.4 miles of out-and-back dirt roads and single track. Heavy Half: 15.4 miles along the same path minus the Ball Mountain section. Minimum age: Marathon 16+\, Heavy Half 14+. Registration SOLD OUT with waitlist available.
LOCATION:135 E. 6th Street\, Leadville\, CO 80461
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:boulder-sunrise-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260628T071500Z
DTEND:20260628T111500Z
SUMMARY:Boulder Sunrise Run
DESCRIPTION:Boulder Sunrise Triathlon at the Boulder Reservoir located at the foot of the Flatirons. A fast triathlon course featuring a swim in the reservoir\, rolling hill bike course with views of the Flatirons\, and a flat run course across the Boulder Reservoir dam. Multiple distance options available including Sprint\, Olympic\, Duathlon\, and Aquabike. Suitable for athletes of all skill levels.
LOCATION:Boulder Reservoir\, Boulder\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:july-4th-freedom-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260704T090000Z
DTEND:20260704T130000Z
SUMMARY:July 4th Freedom Run
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Independence Day with a classic hometown road run starting and ending at Home Plate Bar & Grill. The Freedom Run 5K/10K features neighborhood routes with directional cones marking the courses. Registration includes participant T-shirt\, finisher medal\, awards in 5-year age brackets\, $5 coupon for food/drinks at Home Plate Bar & Grill\, and professional timing. Post-race celebration with awards\, food\, and drinks.
LOCATION:2571 S Koke Mill Rd\, Springfield\, IL 62704
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:loveland-liberty-5k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260704T080000Z
DTEND:20260704T120000Z
SUMMARY:Loveland Liberty 5K
DESCRIPTION:The 12th annual Loveland Liberty 5K hosted by Sweetheart City Racing welcomes both runners and walkers. Features Elite wave (sub-24 min men/sub-26 min women)\, Kids Race (~100 yards)\, and awards for overall\, masters\, and age group winners. Supports Health4Heroes charity. Race begins at 8:15 AM (Elite wave at 8:00 AM). Dogs welcome if leashed (5 feet or shorter).
LOCATION:815 14th Street Southwest\, BLDG B100\, Loveland\, CO 80537
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vail-hillclimb-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260705T070000Z
DTEND:20260705T110000Z
SUMMARY:Vail HillClimb
DESCRIPTION:Trail running race in Vail. Part of the Vail Trail Running Series with aid stations and challenging courses for all ability levels.
LOCATION:Vail Mountain Haus\, 292 E Meadow Dr\, Vail\, CO 81657
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hardrock-hundred-mile-endurance-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260710T080000Z
DTEND:20260710T120000Z
SUMMARY:Hardrock Hundred Mile Endurance Run
DESCRIPTION:100-mile mountain ultramarathon with 33\,264 feet of climb and 33\,264 feet of descent (66\,528 feet total elevation change). Average elevation of 11\,186 feet with low point at 7\,680 feet (Ouray) and high point at 14\,048 feet (Handies Peak). The race traverses the ancestral homeland of the Ute\, Puebloan and Diné people in the San Juan Mountains.
LOCATION:Silverton\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hardrock-100-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260710T080000Z
DTEND:20260710T120000Z
SUMMARY:Hardrock 100
DESCRIPTION:100-mile endurance run with 33\,264 feet of climb and 33\,264 feet of descent (66\,528 feet total elevation change) at an average elevation of 11\,186 feet\, ranging from 7\,680 feet (Ouray) to 14\,048 feet (Handies Peak). The 2026 Runners Manual and Volunteer Manual are live. Event features aid stations\, pacers\, volunteer opportunities\, and community support.
LOCATION:Silverton\, San Juan Mountains\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-silver-rush-50-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260711T060000Z
DTEND:20260711T100000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Silver Rush 50 Run
DESCRIPTION:The Silver Rush 50 Run is a 50-mile out-and-back ultramarathon with 8\,000 feet of elevation gain featuring technical climbs and descents across Leadville's high-altitude terrain under the shadow of 14\,000-foot Rocky Mountain peaks. Also includes a 15-mile run and 5K junior race. Serves as a qualifying event for the LT100 Run.
LOCATION:Base of Dutch Henry Tubing Hill\, US Highway 24 and McWethy Dr\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cookie-chase-5k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260711T080000Z
DTEND:20260711T120000Z
SUMMARY:Cookie Chase 5K
DESCRIPTION:The Cookie Chase 5K takes place at Sloan’s Lake Park\, featuring a scenic course on paved bike trails with views of the Rocky Mountains and Denver skyline. Participants receive a race logo shirt\, a finishers medal\, and fresh cookies at the finish line. The event utilizes wave starts based on estimated finish times and is part of the USATF Colorado Grand Prix.
LOCATION:1700 Utica St\, Denver\, CO 80204
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:silver-rush-50-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260712T060000Z
DTEND:20260712T100000Z
SUMMARY:Silver Rush 50 Run
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Silver Rush 50 Run is a high-altitude 50-mile trail race that takes runners through the historic mining district of Leadville. The out-and-back course reaches elevations of over 12\,000 feet and serves as a qualifier for the Leadville Trail 100 Run.
LOCATION:316 Harrison Ave\, Leadville\, CO 80461
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:diplos-run-club-denver-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260712T090000Z
DTEND:20260712T130000Z
SUMMARY:Diplo's Run Club Denver
DESCRIPTION:5K Run & Rave featuring a run through Denver's iconic neighborhoods starting and finishing at Cheesman Park\, followed by a post-race concert featuring Diplo + friends. Includes packet pick-up on July 11\, festival with main stage lineup\, and music performances.
LOCATION:Cheesman Park\, Denver\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ouray-100-mile-endurance-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260717T080000Z
DTEND:20260717T120000Z
SUMMARY:Ouray 100 Mile Endurance Run
DESCRIPTION:A brutal mountain race with approximately 42\,000 feet of elevation gain for the 100-mile distance. It is known for its steepness and technicality in the heart of the San Juan Mountains.
LOCATION:Fellin Park\, 9th St\, Ouray\, CO 81427
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:high-lonesome-100-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260717T080000Z
DTEND:20260717T120000Z
SUMMARY:High Lonesome 100
DESCRIPTION:A 100-mile high elevation endurance race in the Sawatch Range of the Colorado Rocky Mountains with 23\,500 feet of vertical gain\, reaching 13\,150 feet elevation. The course is a loop through singletrack featuring the National Continental Divide and Colorado Trails\, two ghost towns\, five alpine passes\, remote basins\, and soaring ridges\, completed within 37 hours. Organized by an all-volunteer team as part of Freestone Endurance.
LOCATION:Mount Princeton Hot Springs Resort\, 15870 Co Rd 162\, Nathrop\, CO 81236
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:audi-power-of-four-trail-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260718T080000Z
DTEND:20260718T120000Z
SUMMARY:Audi Power of Four Trail Run
DESCRIPTION:The Audi Power of Four Race Series is a premier endurance race series utilizing the unique terrain of all four Aspen Snowmass mountains. The signature 50K Ultra covers all four mountains via singletrack and dirt road. The 25K runs the Government Trail linking Buttermilk and Snowmass. The 10K starts at Elk Camp Restaurant and traverses Snowmass down to Fanny Hill. Registration fee ranges from $100–$125\, opening January 1st.
LOCATION:Aspen\, Tiehack\, & Elk Camp\, Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:10k-5k-10000-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260718T080000Z
DTEND:20260718T120000Z
SUMMARY:10K & 5K @ 10,000'
DESCRIPTION:High elevation trail running race at 10\,000 feet. Features well-marked routes\, aid stations\, and Skratch Labs hydration support.
LOCATION:Vail\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
