UID:never-summer-100k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260725T053000Z
DTEND:20260725T093000Z
SUMMARY:Never Summer 100K
DESCRIPTION:A true mountain race set in State Forest State Park\, featuring rugged alpine ridge running and technically challenging singletrack. The course travels between the Never Summer and Medicine Bow Mountains\, offering constant views of rocky peaks and high alpine lakes.
LOCATION:Gould Community Center\, 56750 CO-14\, Walden\, CO 80480
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wild-west-relay-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260731T050000Z
DTEND:20260731T090000Z
SUMMARY:Wild West Relay
DESCRIPTION:A scenic point-to-point running relay adventure across Colorado starting in Fort Collins and finishing 200 miles away in Steamboat Springs. Teams of 1-12 runners compete on July 31 - August 1\, 2026. Multiple team categories available: 12-person teams ($2\,975.40)\, Ultra teams 4-6 runners ($1\,706.60)\, Super Ultra teams 1-3 runners ($925)\, and High School teams ($1\,101.32). Race features mountain passes\, open spaces\, and road running with GPS tracking and volunteer support along the course.
LOCATION:Budweiser Brewing Plant (Anheuser Busch Facility)\, Fort Collins\, CO 80524
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rocky-mountain-half-marathon-5k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260731T180000Z
DTEND:20260731T220000Z
SUMMARY:Rocky Mountain Half Marathon & 5K
DESCRIPTION:A challenging but scenic run just outside Rocky Mountain National Park. The 5K runs on a counterclockwise loop around Lake Estes with an aggressive initial climb followed by mostly downhill terrain. The half marathon (August 1) starts and ends by the lake at the fairgrounds in historic Estes Park\, Colorado\, featuring killer mountain views\, elevation gain of +1\,267 ft\, and a 4.5-hour cutoff time.
LOCATION:Stanley Park Ball Field\, Estes Park\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rocky-mountain-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260801T060000Z
DTEND:20260801T100000Z
SUMMARY:Rocky Mountain Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:A challenging but scenic race just outside Rocky Mountain National Park\, starting and finishing near Lake Estes at the fairgrounds in historic Estes Park\, Colorado. The weekend event includes a 5K on Friday evening (July 31) and a Half Marathon on Saturday morning (August 1). An 'Elk Double' challenge option is available for runners who complete both distances. The half marathon features a paved road loop with +1\,267 ft / -1\,263 ft elevation change and a 4-hour time limit. The 5K is a counterclockwise loop around Lake Estes with +156 ft elevation. Stunning views of the Continental Divide and Rocky Mountain National Park throughout.
LOCATION:Stanley Park Ball Field\, Estes Park\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
