BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:san-juan-softie-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260814T060000Z
DTEND:20260814T100000Z
SUMMARY:San Juan Softie
DESCRIPTION:The San Juan Softie is a 100-mile ultramarathon (~104 miles) starting and finishing just north of Durango\, Colorado. The course traverses stunning and rugged terrain including the Colorado Trail\, Engineer Mountain\, Wilson group of 14ers\, and Lizard Head. Features ~19\,000 ft of total elevation gain\, an average elevation of 10\,282 ft\, and a 38-hour cutoff (6:00 AM Friday start to 8:00 PM Saturday finish). The 2026 event is SOLD OUT with a waitlist available. Required gear includes rain jacket\, 2 light sources\, gloves\, whistle\, hat\, water capacity\, cup/bowl\, and satellite tracking device. Cash prizes offered: $500/1st\, $250/2nd\, $100/3rd for men and women.
LOCATION:Durango\, CO (start/finish just north of Durango)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-10k-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260815T060000Z
DTEND:20260815T100000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 10K
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 MTB is one of the most prestigious endurance cross-country mountain bike events in the world. Riders tackle a grueling 105.3-mile out-and-back course through the Colorado Rockies with 12\,304 feet of elevation gain\, starting at 10\,152 feet and reaching a peak elevation of 12\,500 feet at Columbine Mine. The race includes steep climbs\, technical descents\, and high alpine terrain. Riders have 12 hours to complete the race to earn a belt buckle.
LOCATION:Corner of 6th St & Harrison\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mt-sneffels-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
