BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leadville-trail-100-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260822T040000Z
DTEND:20260822T080000Z
SUMMARY:Leadville Trail 100 Run
DESCRIPTION:The Life Time Leadville Trail 100 RUN presented by La Sportiva is one of the oldest and most storied endurance running events in the world. This 100-mile out-and-back ultramarathon starts at 10\,200 feet and climbs to 12\,500 feet (Hope Pass) in the Colorado Rockies. The race features over 15\,000 feet of elevation gain across brutal terrain including steep climbs\, high-altitude passes\, and technical Colorado Trail sections. Finishers under 25 hours receive the big buckle; those under 30 hours receive the small buckle.
LOCATION:Corner of 6th St & Harrison\, Leadville\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:staunton-rocks-marathon-half-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T000000Z
DTSTART:20260822T070000Z
DTEND:20260822T110000Z
SUMMARY:Staunton Rocks! Marathon & Half
DESCRIPTION:An event put on by trail runners for trail runners\, touring the renowned singletrack of Staunton State Park in Colorado's Front Range Mountains southwest of Denver. The marathon features 26.3 miles with 4\,500 feet of vertical gain (90% singletrack\, 10% dirt road)\, while the half marathon is 13.1 miles with 2\,200 feet of vertical gain. Runners will experience historic buildings\, old milling operations\, flowing trails\, technical features\, 60+ mile views from overlooks\, scenic lakes and streams. Elevation ranges from 8\,200' to 9\,500'. Registration capped at 150 for each distance with 10-hour cutoff for marathon and 9-hour cutoff for half marathon.
LOCATION:Staunton State Park\, Pine\, Colorado
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
